From: MeowArchMobile adbd standalone build
Subject: [PATCH] main.cpp: honor ADBD_NO_AUTH on non-Android hosts

auth_required defaults to true and only Android's ro.adb.secure /
userdebug logic ever clears it. A glibc host has no framework to approve
keys, so give it an escape hatch: ADBD_NO_AUTH=1 disables adbd-side
authentication entirely.

--- a/daemon/main.cpp
+++ b/daemon/main.cpp
@@ -235,6 +235,11 @@ int adbd_main() {
 #endif
 #endif
 
+#if !defined(__ANDROID__)
+    // No framework to approve keys on a glibc host; allow opt-out entirely.
+    if (getenv("ADBD_NO_AUTH")) auth_required = false;
+#endif
+
     // Our external storage path may be different than apps, since
     // we aren't able to bind mount after dropping root.
     const char* adb_external_storage = getenv("ADB_EXTERNAL_STORAGE");
